Travel is great but traveling can be a  struggle to help you navigate this kind  of traveling we pulled together a  mountain of data across seven different  categories and ranked nine major US  airlines from best to worst by basing  our stats on the percentage of flights  and passengers with problems we were  able to compare Airlines of all sizes  and that way we were able to truly say  which is the best airlines of 2019 and  which performed the worst Delta was the  most punctual airline in 2019  it's on-time rate including  international flights and regional  partners was eighty-three percent two  full percentage points ahead of Alaska  which was also significant since most  airlines had a tougher year last year in  terms of on-time arrivals in last place  frontier at 73% ever been stuck on the  tarmac  some times it probably feels like a  special circle in Dante's Inferno at  least Southwest had the lowest rate of  flight stuck on the tarmac for two hours  or more mishandled baggage is its own  frustrating discovery once you touch  down of all airlines Allegiant  mishandled bags least frequently while  American was the most likely to lose or  delay your checked luggage anyone who  lives with particularly rough winters or  overcrowded airports is no stranger to  extreme delays meaning a delay of 45  minutes or more so it's worth noting  that Alaska was the best in this  category with the lowest rate of extreme  delays  whereas JetBlue came in last place in  this category and of course the cause of  groans that echo through the terminals  of every airport the infuriating  canceled flight Delta made the top of  the list with the lowest rate of  canceled flights American was three  times more likely to cancel the flight  than Delta getting involuntary bump can  be gut-wrenching for passengers you have  a ticket you need to get somewhere and  the airline says sorry you have to go  much later  that means more gates sitting  it's no fun unless there's a Cinnabon  nearby 